// Every field read from the datasheet: Table 1 "VDS 100 V", "ID 256 A" (the product page's
// parametric table says 180 A at 25 °C; Table 1's 256 A is carried because it is the datasheet's own
// key-parameter figure), "Type/Ordering Code IPB017N10N5LF / Package PG-TO263-7 / Marking 017N10LF",
// the title "OptiMOS 5 Linear FET, 100V", and the first feature bullet. Table 1 also characterizes the
// pulse current at "VDS=56V, tp=10 ms" -- a datasheet choosing 56 V for its linear-mode figure is the
// vendor's own statement of the bus it designs the part for, and is carried as such below.
data ipb017n10n5lf: ElectronicComponentRow = ElectronicComponentRow {
  vendor: infineon,
  ordering_code: "IPB017N10N5LF",
  package: "PG-TO263-7 (D2PAK 7-pin)",
  top_marking: "017N10LF",
  voltage_rating: ComponentVoltageRating { kind: DrainSourceMaximum, maximum: volt(count: 100) },
  current_rating: ampere(count: 256),
  vendor_application_statements: [
    "OptiMOS 5 Linear FET, 100V",
    "Ideal for hot-swap and e-fuse applications",
    "Wide safe operating area SOA",
    "Ipulse (VDS=56V, tp=10 ms) 10.2 A",
  ],
}
